  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{5}$ from the denominator, we need to multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{5},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{2(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{2\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
